    board: file CF-075 — node-create never stages the disk-floor resolver, so every documented node creation dies on its first layer
    
    Measured at origin/main ee0a06d by the code-factory-dogfood lane while walking the README
    quick start literally. scripts/node-create.sh:43-47 copies three files into the node
    (project-node.sh, lib.sh, harness/install-<harness>.sh); scripts/project-node.sh:64 executes
    "$HERE/disk_floor.py", which node-create.sh never copies, so the entry point dies before any
    layer runs.
    
    Live evidence (reachable host, zero credentials staged, ttl 1h, agent destroyed and censused
    after): spawn PASS, staged PASS, then inside the node
      python3: can't open file '.../node-scripts/disk_floor.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory
      NODE: FAIL (disk floor)
      FAIL provision — node reported FAIL
      NODE INCOMPLETE (2), rc=1
    The same failure reproduces with no bunker host by staging exactly node-create's file set into
    a temp dir (the row's probe field carries the one-line command; it was executed as written at
    this commit). The agent the failed create spawned stayed alive until destroyed by hand with an
    explicit --server; that cleanup gap is acceptance criterion 4 of the row.
    
    Distinct from CF-056 (stage-2 cannot FAIL: swallowed cp exit statuses) — here every cp
    succeeds and the staged SET is incomplete, so an exit-status fix alone would not catch it.
    
