03` by hand (home 246.7 MB) and a follow-up `bunker info` census returned not_found. Distinct from CF-056 (node-create stage-2 cannot FAIL because cp exit statuses are swallowed): here every cp succeeds and the staged SET is incomplete, so an exit-status fix alone would not notice this. Distinct from CF-041 (quick-start env/arg defects, closed) and CF-040 (build cache).","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree from the repo root: the `probe` field prints `python3: can't open file '.../disk_floor.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory` followed by `NODE: FAIL (disk floor)` and exits 1 today.\n1. node-create.sh stages every file project-node.sh executes at runtime — at minimum disk_floor.py — and the staged set is derived rather than hand-maintained (copy the scripts the entry point references, or stage scripts/ as a unit). A check on the staged set exits nonzero when any referenced file is missing; `grep -c disk_floor.py scripts/node-create.sh` is non-zero and a selftest fixture fails if it ever returns to 0.\n2. The hermetic staging probe continues past the disk floor and prints a NAMED row for it (PASS or WARN with the measured GiB and its source), never a bare interpreter error, and the run reaches the remaining layers.\n3. A live node creation against a reachable host shows no 'can't open file' line; its fail structure matches the control-host run (crier_identity and inference-key rows may still FAIL — this row is about staging, not about a node being complete).\n4. A failed provision leaves no live agent behind: node-create.sh destroys the agent it spawned when the run ends FAIL, or prints the exact `bunker destroy <id> --server <host>` command it requires; a post-failure `bunker info <id> --server <host>` census shows not_found or the named command is in the output.\n5. tests/selftest.sh gains a fixture that stages node-create's file set into a temp dir and asserts no unhandled interpreter error plus the named disk-floor row; `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` at the fixed tip.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/harness\" \"$d/home\"; cp scripts/project-node.sh scripts/lib.sh \"$d/\"; cp scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh \"$d/harness/\"; chmod +x \"$d/project-node.sh\"; HOME=\"$d/home\" \"$d/project-node.sh\" --apply --project cfprobe --harness hermes --repo https://github.com/github/gitignore; echo rc=$?","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:12:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:12:00Z"}
